## Model card

- **Name:** Neomorph
- **Short description:** Local metadata describes Neomorph as an OpenCode Zen experimental model (64K context, $0.50/$1.50 per 1M tokens, text in/out) with a modular sub-network architecture and structured-output focus, but no independently verifiable official/public model documentation was located in this pass.
- **Provider / access:** Claimed as OpenCode Zen / `opencode/neomorph` in local metadata. No verifiable listing found in reviewed OpenCode Go/Console model docs, models.dev API/search, OpenRouter API/search, Artificial Analysis search, or Hugging Face search for this exact identity.
- **Release / knowledge:** Experimental/unannounced in accessible public sources reviewed. Release date and knowledge cutoff not independently verified.
- **IDs:** `neomorph`, `opencode/neomorph` (local metadata claims).
- **Context window:** 64,000 tokens total; 4,096 max output (local metadata claim, unverified).
- **Modalities:** Text input/output (local metadata claim, unverified).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-14):** $0.50/$1.50 per 1M in/out (local metadata/provider-documentation claim, unverified in accessible official public sources).
- **Architecture:** Proprietary/experimental “modular sub-network architecture” per local metadata; parameter count and detailed architecture not publicly verified.

